# The Dockerfile COPYs whole directories (backend, packages/*) into the
# build stage — without this file, `COPY backend backend` would also copy
# backend/.env (real MONGODB_URI/JWT_SECRET/GROQ_API_KEY/RESEND_API_KEY)
# into an image layer. Multi-stage build discards that layer from the final
# image, but it would still exist in the build stage and any pushed/cached
# layer, so real secrets must never enter the build context at all.
.env
.env.*
!.env.example

node_modules
**/node_modules
dist
**/dist
.next
coverage
.git
.claude
*.log
